pdated\":null,\"date_updated\":null,\"open_in_new_tab\":true,\"search_page\":{\"id\":\"35f4ad04-4108-4a83-9823-a37683e87f90\",\"sort\":16,\"date_created\":\"2026-10-11T17:33:57.530Z\",\"user_created\":\"211f17e7-d30c-4260-909a-156da2993df4\",\"date_updated\":\"2026-11-11T09:31:25.864Z\",\"user_updated\":\"211f17e7-d30c-4260-909a-156da2993df4\",\"title\":\"Search Result\",\"status\":\"published\",\"published_at\":null,\"seo\":{\"title\":\"Search Result\",\"meta_description\":null},\"permalink\":\"/search\",\"parent\":null,\"short_headline\":null,\"newsroom_circulars_date_of_publication\":null,\"postal_code\":null,\"newsroom_image\":null,\"thumbnail\":null,\"is_show_last_updated\":false,\"select_template\":497,\"feedback\":null,\"note_for_approvers\":null,\"total_page_view_count\":460464,\"page_type\":\"standard\",\"redirect_page\":null,\"redirect_url\":null,\"should_open_in_new_window\":false,\"additional_urls\":[],\"format_publish_date\":\"Published At: Oct 19th, 2026 12:02\",\"override_default_template_blocks\":true,\"date_published_at\":null,\"time_published_at\":\"00:00:00\",\"countries_and_regions\":[],\"circular_status\":[],\"blocks\":[\"b0691d21-b34d-48f7-b6be-4353691fbf5d\"],\"view_roles\":[],\"content_types\":[],\"raag_filter_subtype\":[],\"edit_roles\":[99815,99816],\"topics\":[],\"featured_article_tagging\":[],\"profile_and_topic\":[],\"commodity_type\":[],\"template_block\":[],\"create_roles\":[]}},\"blockId\":8865,\"itemId\":595,\"pageId\":\"$undefined\",\"detailData\":\"$undefined\",\"lastUpdated\":\"$D2026-11-12T04:44:56.271Z\",\"pageTitle\":\"$undefined\",\"current_permalink\":\"$undefined\"}]\n45:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"col-12 col-lg-3 article-content-right\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"layout-right-related sf_colsIn\",\"data-sf-element\":\"Sticky Area\",\"data-placeholder-label\":\"Sticky Area\",\"children\":[\"$L75\"]}]}]\n46:[\"$\",\"$L76\",null,{}]\n78:T40c,\u003chtml\u003e\u003chead\u003e\u003c/head\u003e\u003cbody\u003e\u003ch2\u003eHow do these import requirements ensure the food safety of Fish \u0026amp; Fish Products?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eSFA adopts a science and risk-based approach to ensure that food is safe for consumption in Singapore. The requirements imposed ensure food safety and reduce the risk of foodborne illnesses.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cp\u003eMore requirements are imposed on high-risk Fish \u0026amp; Fish Products.\u0026nbsp;For example, frozen oysters require health certificates as they are more susceptible to microbiological and chemical contamination.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf you intend to import live oysters, you will need to obtain a health certificate as well as from countries/regions that meet SFA’s requirements for a shellfish sanitation programme. This is because live oysters pose a higher risk than frozen ones.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe labelling requirements also provide consumers with the information to make informed choices. It also improves traceability in the event of food safety issues or recalls.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/body\u003e\u003c/html\u003e79:T416,\u003chtml\u003e\u003chead\u003e\u003c/head\u003e\u003cbody\u003e\u003cp\u003eEvery container (e.g. carton or basket) of fruits or vegetables \u003cstrong\u003emust \u003c/strong\u003ebe labelled with the following:\u2028\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003ename and address of the producer\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003eproduct description\u003c/li\u003e\u003cli\u003edate of export/packing\u2028\u003c/li\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"callout-type\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"tip-notification\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://assets.app.optical.gov.sg/sfa/production/published/collections/pages/%252Ffood-import-export%252Fcommercial-imports%252Fimport-requirements-for-food-food-products/18ebc740-fefb-4062-b132-b8c48257dc52.svg\" alt=\"Icon Tip\" title=\"Icon Success Notification\"\u003e\u2028 \u003cdiv class=\"notification-content\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou must inform your supplier or exporter to comply with the SFA's labelling requirements. \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor more details, see\u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/regulatory-standards-frameworks-guidelines/food-labelling-packaging-guidelines/labelling-requirements-for-food\" sfref=\"[f669d9a7-009d-4d83-ddaa-000000000002]b1dd1acf-5300-475b-b2ec-80fec75de1ca\"\u003e Labelling Requirements for Food\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/body\u003e\u003c/html\u003e7a:T40c,\u003chtml\u003e\u003chead\u003e\u003c/head\u003e\u003cbody\u003e\u003ch2\u003eWhat are Processed Food \u0026amp; Food Contact Articles?\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eProcessed Food refers to products such as biscuits, cooking oil and mineral water. \u003c/p\u003eA Food Contact Article refers to an item that is designed for use in, or in connection with the handling of food or beverages that comes into contact with food or beverages and does not require electricity to function. Examples include plates, bowls, cups, straws, pots and utensils such as chopsticks and spoons.\u0026nbsp;\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo check whether your product falls under this category, please use the \u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/tools-and-resources/food-and-related-products-classification-tool\"\u003eFood and Related Products Classification Tool\u003c/a\u003e. To learn more about the different categories of food and food products, please see the \u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/food-import-export/general-classification-of-food-food-products/classification-of-general-food-food-products\"\u003eClassification of General Food \u0026amp; Food Products.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/body\u003e\u003c/html\u003e7b:Ta7f,\u003ch2\u003eWhat is needed to import Processed Food \u0026amp; Food Contact Articles for sale?\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe sale of Processed Food \u0026amp; Food Contact Articles is governed under the Sale of Food Act 1973 and Food Regulations.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAll pre-packed food products for sale in Singapore should meet requirements specified in Part 3 of the Food Regulations. For more information, please see \u003ca href=\"/regulatory-standards-frameworks-guidelines/food-labelling-packaging-guidelines/labelling-requirements-for-food\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eLabelling Guidelines for Food\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnly permitted food additives and ingredients are allowed in food. Please check the relevant requirements here:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sfa-text-link\" style=\"color: rgb(220, 68, 5); font-weight: 600;\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.sfa.gov.sg/regulatory-standards-frameworks-guidelines/food-safety-regulatory-limits/regulatory-limits-for-food-additives\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eRegulatory Limits for Food Additives\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sfa-text-link\" style=\"color: rgb(220, 68, 5); font-weight: 600;\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.sfa.gov.sg/regulatory-standards-frameworks-guidelines/food-safety-regulatory-limits/regulatory-limits-for-contaminants-in-food\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eRegulatory Limits for Contaminants in Food\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sfa-text-link\" style=\"color: rgb(220, 68, 5); font-weight: 600;\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.sfa.gov.sg/regulatory-standards-frameworks-guidelines/ingredients-used-in-food/chinese-medicinal-materials-and-ingredients-used-in-food\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"\u003eChinese Medicinal Materials and Ingredients Used in Food\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAll imported Processed Food and Food Contact Articles need to be accompanied by a valid permit under Regulation of Imports and Exports Regulations Section 3.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou should check on the requirements for your food product before you\u0026nbsp;\u003ca href=\"/food-import-export/commercial-imports/what-you-need-to-know-for-import-of-food\"\u003eapply for a permit\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;to import Processed Food \u0026amp; Food Contact Articles into Singapore.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor processed foods like infant formulas and ready-to-eat food, importers are to provide additional supporting documents. Please refer to the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca style=\"font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; text-transform: inherit; word-spacing: normal; white-space: inherit;\" title=\"Import Requirements of Specific Food Products\" href=\"/api/assets/fa89c526-e82d-4e62-b5cd-581d1b95d9e5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" aria-label=\"Requirements of Specific Food Products Imported for Sale\"\u003eDocuments needed for the sale of Specific Food Products\u003c/a\u003e\u0026nbsp;for the details.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e7c:Ta04,\u003chtml\u003e\u003chead\u003e\u003c/head\u003e\u003cbody\u003e\u003ch2\u003e\u003cb style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); color: inherit; font-size: var(--font-size-h4); text-align: inherit; text-transform: inherit; word-spacing: normal; caret-color: auto; white-space: inherit\"\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003ci\u003eEnhanced Regulated Source Programme\u003c/i\u003e (imports from Malaysia)\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ch2\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn addition to the supporting documents required for specific food products listed above, the \u003ci\u003eEnhanced Regulated Source Programme \u003c/i\u003erequires processed food imported \u003cb\u003efrom Malaysia\u003c/b\u003e to come from registered establishments.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe following food products are covered under the programme. You are required to submit documents showing that your food products are obtained from registered establishments.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003ctable style=\"width: 844px\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr style=\"height: 16.6666666666667%\"\u003e\u003cth style=\"width: 6.46501%\" data-role=\"resizable\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eNo.\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth style=\"width: 93%\"\u003e\u003cb\u003eTypes of Products\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr style=\"height: 16.6666666666667%\"\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width: 6.46501%\"\u003e1\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width: 93.535%\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eInfant formula\u003c/p\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"callout-type\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"to-note\"\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou can use the  \u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/assets/a696d541-6cf9-49b3-80d0-eb06095f0b22\" aria-label=\"Calculation Guide for Infant Formula (Excel sheet)\"\u003eCalculation guide for infant formula\u003c/a\u003e to ensure the nutritional composition is within the limits. \u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr style=\"height: 16.6666666666667%\"\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width: 6.46501%\"\u003e2\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width: 93.535%\"\u003eInfant Cereal\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr style=\"height: 16.6666666666667%\"\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width: 6.46501%\"\u003e3\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd\u003e\u003cp\u003eTraditional cakes/kueh kueh, cooked rice products, and other perishable cooked food that are ready-to-eat.\u0026nbsp;Frozen and/or uncooked products are currently excluded. \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor more information, see\u0026nbsp;\u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/api/assets/87e4aaf6-bb09-4586-b032-58632955bab0\" aria-label=\"Examples of Traditional Cakes (Kueh Kueh), Cooked Rice Products and Other Perishable Cooked Food\"\u003eExamples of Traditional Cakes (Kueh Kueh), Cooked Rice Products and Other Perishable Cooked Food\u003c/a\u003e.\u2028\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr style=\"height: 16.6666666666667%\"\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width: 6.46501%\"\u003e4\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width: 93.535%\"\u003eMooncakes\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr style=\"height: 16.6666666666667%\"\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width: 6.46501%\"\u003e5\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width: 93.535%\"\u003eDried beancurd sticks, skin, and sheets\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr style=\"height: 16.6666666666667%\"\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width: 6.46501%\"\u003e6\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width: 93.535%\"\u003eEdible oil\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/body\u003e\u003c/html\u003e7d:T124b,\u003chtml\u003e\u003chead\u003e\u003c/head\u003e\u003cbody\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"table-text sf_colsIn\" data-sf-element=\"Text Table - Content Block\" =\"\"=\"\" data-placeholder-label=\"Text Table - Content Block\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"sfContentBlock sf-Long-text\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"table-wrap\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"table-wrap-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\"\u003e\u2028 \u003cp\u003eIf your processed food product falls under this programme, you must submit documentary proof to SFA that your processed food products are from registered establishments before applying for an import permit.\u003c/p\u003e\u2028 \u003cp\u003eFollow the steps below to submit your documents and obtain the establishment code.\u2028\u2028                \u003c/p\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"table-text sf_colsIn\" data-sf-element=\"Text Table - Content Block\" data-placeholder-label=\"Text Table - Content Block\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"sfContentBlock sf-Long-text\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"table-wrap\"\u003e\u2028 \u2028                        \u2028                            \u2028                            \u2028                        \u2028                        \u2028                            \u2028                            \u2028                        \u2028                        \u2028                            \u2028                            \u2028                        \u2028                        \u2028                            \u2028                            \u2028                        \u2028                        \u2028                            \u2028                            \u2028                        \u2028                    \u2028\u003cdiv class=\"table-wrap-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"table-wrap\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"table-wrap-scroll\" tabindex=\"0\"\u003e\u003ctable style=\"height:74.5px;width:518.667px;\"\u003e\u003ctbody\u003e\u003ctr style=\"height:30.1887%;\"\u003e\u003cth style=\"width:8.83337%;\" data-role=\"resizable\"\u003eNo.\u003c/th\u003e\u003cth style=\"width:91.1667%;\"\u003eSteps\u003c/th\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr style=\"height:35.2201%;\"\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width:8.83337%;\"\u003e1\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width:91.1667%;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEnsure you are importing from registered Malaysian establishments\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u2028 \u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003eRegistered Malaysian establishments are food manufacturing establishments that have been registered with the Malaysian Ministry of Health (MOH).\u003c/p\u003e\u2028 \u003cp\u003ePlease contact MOH Malaysia for details:\u003c/p\u003e\u2028 \u003cp\u003eFood Safety \u0026amp; Quality Division, Ministry of Health Malaysia\u003cbr\u003e(Attn: Ms Norshafawati Binti Rosli)\u2028                                    \u003cbr\u003eTel: +60-03-8885 0797 ext 4074\u003cbr\u003eEmail: \u003ca href=\"mailto:norshafawati@moh.gov.my\"\u003enorshafawati@moh.gov.my\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExport Branch\u003c/p\u003e\u2028\u2028\u2028\u2028\u2028 \u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr style=\"height:35.2201%;\"\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width:8.83337%;\"\u003e2\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width:91.1667%;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eObtain documentary proof\u003c/strong\u003e\u2028 \u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003eYou must gather the following documents before you can import food or food products under this programme:\u003cbr\u003e\u2028\u2028\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eMOH Malaysia registration letter\u2028                                    \u003c/li\u003e\u2028 \u003cli\u003einvoices from the establishment\u003c/li\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/ul\u003e\u2028\u2028\u2028\u2028\u003cdiv class=\"callout-type\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"to-note\"\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003eThis step can take a month or longer, depending on how quickly you can gather the required documents from your supplier.\u2028                                            \u003c/li\u003e\u2028 \u003cli\u003eRetain the original documents as you will need to produce them for SFA inspections.\u003c/li\u003e\u2028\u003c/ul\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr style=\"height:35.2201%;\"\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width:8.83337%;\"\u003e3\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width:91.1667%;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSubmit documentary proof\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u2028\u2028 \u003cp\u003eDocuments must be submitted before you import a processed food product. \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003ePlease submit the documents using the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://csp.sfa.gov.sg/feedback\"\u003eSFA Online Feedback Form\u003c/a\u003e.\u2028 \u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003ctr style=\"height:35.2201%;\"\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width:8.83337%;\"\u003e4\u003c/td\u003e\u003ctd style=\"width:91.1667%;\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eReceive establishment code\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u2028 \u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003c/strong\u003eIf your submission is in order, you will receive an establishment code (e.g. MYZNNV0001) for each manufacturer upon submission of the documents.\u003c/p\u003e\u2028 \u003cp\u003eYou will need this code to fill in the CA/SC Code1 field when applying for your import permit through TradeNet.\u003c/p\u003e\u2028 \u003cp\u003eYou will also be required to submit the following documents for each import consignment:\u003cbr\u003e\u2028\u2028\u003c/p\u003e\u003cul\u003e\u003cli\u003einvoices\u2028 \u003c/li\u003e\u2028 \u003cli\u003epacking lists\u003c/li\u003e\u2028 \u003cli\u003emanufacturer’s licences\u003c/li\u003e\u2028 \u003c/ul\u003eFor details on import permits, see \u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/food-import-export/licence-permit--registration/application-process--fees-for-licence-permit-registration-for-import-export\" sfref=\"[f669d9a7-009d-4d83-ddaa-000000000002]510b4efc-0247-4167-b309-30556cb3cf69\"\u003eApplication Process \u0026amp; Fees for Licence / Permit / Registration for Import / Export\u003c/a\u003e.\u2028\u003cbr\u003e\u2028 \u003c/td\u003e\u003c/tr\u003e\u003c/tbody\u003e\u003c/table\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/body\u003e\u003c/html\u003e7e:T4cb,\u003chtml\u003e\u003chead\u003e\u003c/head\u003e\u003cbody\u003e\u003ch2\u003e\u003cb style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); color: inherit; font-size: var(--font-size-h4); text-align: inherit; text-transform: inherit; word-spacing: normal; caret-color: auto; white-space: inherit\"\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003ci\u003e\u003c/i\u003eReady-to-Eat Minimally Processed (MP) Cut/ Peeled Fruits (including coconuts), Vegetables and Cut Sugarcane from Malaysia\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ch2\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eTo import \u003cb\u003eReady-to-Eat\u003c/b\u003e minimally processed cut/peeled fruits (including coconuts), vegetables and cut sugarcane from Malaysia, you are required to submit documents showing that it is obtained from producers registered and certified by Malaysian Ministry of Health.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe registration process is the same as the \u003ci style=\"background-color: initial; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; text-transform: inherit; word-spacing: normal; caret-color: auto; white-space: inherit\"\u003eEnhanced Regulated Source Programme\u003c/i\u003e. Please refer to the \u003ca href=\"#ready-to-eat\" data-sf-ec-immutable=\"\"\u003eabove section\u003c/a\u003e \u003ci style=\"background-color: initial; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; text-transform: inherit; word-spacing: normal; caret-color: auto; white-space: inherit\"\u003e\u003c/i\u003efor information.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/body\u003e\u003c/html\u003e7f:T590,\u003chtml\u003e\u003chead\u003e\u003c/head\u003e\u003cbody\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf your submission is in order, you will receive a unique establishment code (e.g. AUZGxxxx) for each registered supplier from SFA\u0026nbsp;\u003cstrong\u003ewithin 2 weeks\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp style=\"line-height:120%;\"\u003eYou will need this code to fill in CA/SC Code1 field when \u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/food-import-export/commercial-imports/what-you-need-to-know-for-import-of-food#import-permit\"\u003eapplying for your import permit\u003c/a\u003e through TradeNet. For details on import permits, see \u003c/p\u003e\u003cp style=\"line-height:120%;\"\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/food-import-export/commercial-imports/what-you-need-to-know-for-import-of-food\" sfref=\"[f669d9a7-009d-4d83-ddaa-000000000002]12e361ce-96f7-47c1-bc13-c35c9c951eda\" style=\"text-decoration: none;\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sfa-text-link\" style=\"color: rgb(220, 68, 5); font-family: OpenSans-SemiBold;\"\u003eWhat You Need to Know for Import of Food for Commercial Sale\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp style=\"line-height:120%;\"\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/food-import-export/licence-permit-registration/application-process-fees-for-licence-permit-registration-for-import-export\" sfref=\"[f669d9a7-009d-4d83-ddaa-000000000002|lng%3Aen]510b4efc-0247-4167-b309-30556cb3cf69\" style=\"text-decoration: none;\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sfa-text-link\" style=\"color: rgb(220, 68, 5); font-family: OpenSans-SemiBold;\"\u003eApplication Process \u0026amp; Fees for Licence / Permit / Registration for Import / Export\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/body\u003e\u003c/html\u003e80:T4da,\u003chtml\u003e\u003chead\u003e\u003c/head\u003e\u003cbody\u003e\u003ch2\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e\u003ch2\u003eGuidelines to Import Insects \u0026amp; Insect Products\u003c/h2\u003e\u003cp\u003eSFA’s priority is to ensure the safety of food consumed in Singapore. As the insect industry is nascent and insects are a new food item here, SFA has developed the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/regulatory-standards-frameworks-guidelines/insect-regulatory-framework/insect-regulatory-framework\"\u003einsect regulatory framework\u003c/a\u003e, which puts in place guidelines for insects to be approved as food.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eFor imports of insects and insect products for human consumption, importers should register with SFA for the \u003ca href=\"https://www.gobusiness.gov.sg/browse-all-licences/singapore-food-agency-(sfa)/registration-to-import-processed-food-products-and-food-appliances\" target=\"_blank\" data-sf-ec-immutable=\"\"\u003eRegistration to import processed food and food appliances\u003c/a\u003e.\u0026nbsp;Insects and insect products may be imported from any country or region as long as the imported insect and insect products meet SFA’s guidelines.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe following guidelines will apply to the import of insects and insect products, depending on their intended purpose (i.e. production for human consumption or animal feed for food-producing animals).\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/body\u003e\u003c/html\u003e81:T554,\u003chtml\u003e\u003chead\u003e\u003c/head\u003e\u003cbody\u003e\u003cp\u003eBefore importing any food or food product, please ensure that all food additives and ingredients included in the product are permitted under SFA’s Food Regulations.\u0026nbsp;\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003ePlease refer to the following pages for information:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/regulatory-standards-frameworks-guidelines/food-safety-regulatory-limits/overview-on-food-safety-regulatory-limits\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sfa-text-link\"\u003eOverview on Food Safety Regulatory Limits\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sfa-text-link\"\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/regulatory-standards-frameworks-guidelines/food-safety-regulatory-limits/regulatory-limits-for-food-additives\"\u003eRegulatory Limits for Food Additives\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sfa-text-link\"\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/regulatory-standards-frameworks-guidelines/food-safety-regulatory-limits/regulatory-limits-for-contaminants-in-food\"\u003eRegulatory Limits for Contaminants in Food\u003cfont color=\"#dc4405\" size=\"-1\" style=\"background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); text-align: inherit; text-transform: inherit; word-spacing: normal; caret-color: auto\"\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003c/font\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/regulatory-standards-frameworks-guidelines/ingredients-used-in-food/chinese-medicinal-materials-and-ingredients-used-in-food\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sfa-text-link\"\u003eChinese Medicinal Materials and ingredients used in food\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/body\u003e\u003c/html\u003e82:T559,\u003chtml\u003e\u003chead\u003e\u003c/head\u003e\u003cbody\u003e\u003cp\u003ePlease refer to the following pages for information:\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sfa-text-link\"\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" href=\"/regulatory-standards-frameworks-guidelines/genetically-engineered-food-and-feed/regulatory-framework-for-the-use-of-genome-edited-crops-in-food-and-or-animal-feed\"\u003eRegulatory framework for the use of genome edited crops in food and/or animal feed\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e \u003ca href=\"/regulatory-standards-frameworks-guidelines/genetically-engineered-food-and-feed/conditions-related-to-use-of-genetically-modified-crops-in-food\" target=\"_blank\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sfa-text-link\"\u003eConditions related to use of genetically modified crops in food\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sfa-text-link\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"/regulatory-standards-frameworks-guidelines/genetically-engineered-food-and-feed/regulatory-framework-for-the-use-of-genome-edited-crops-in-food-and-or-animal-feed\" target=\"_blank\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003ca href=\"/regulatory-standards-frameworks-guidelines/genetically-engineered-food-and-feed/labelling-requirements-for-genetically-modified-food\" style=\"font-family: inherit; font-style: inherit; font-weight: inherit; font-size: inherit; text-align: inherit; text-transform: inherit; word-spacing: normal; white-space: inherit; caret-color: auto; display: inline !important\" target=\"_blank\"\u003eLabelling Requirements for Genetically Modified (GM) Food\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/body\u003e\u003c/html\u003e2b:[\"$\",\"$L77\",null,{\"sections\":[{\"id\":\"28e8fa83-2111-4976-ae42-066eafc2107d\",\"sort\":1,\"page\":\"28b71ddc-5947-40be-af6e-eac9dad0f496\",\"collection\":\"Sfacorp_AnnouncementBannerBlock\",\"hide_block\":false,\"background\":\"light\",\"date_created\":\"2026-10-11T18:01:45.200Z\",\"user_created\":\"211f17e7-d30c-4260-909a-156da2993df4\",\"date_updated\":null,\"user_updated\":null,\"item\":{\"id\":794,\"sort\":null,\"user_created\":\"211f17e7-d30c-4260-909a-156da2993df4\",\"date_created\":\"2026-10-11T18:01:45.194Z\",\"user_updated\":null,\"date_updated\":null,\"feedback\":null,\"announcements\":[]}},{\"id\":\"28313364-4c9d-483b-951d-3b8ac1e4b94c\",\"sort\":2,\"page\":\"28b71ddc-5947-40be-af6e-eac9dad0f496\",\"collection\":\"Sfacorp_Column93\",\"hi